Forager patch 0004: a mark in the barriers layer of every zoom-15 tile (dispatch 2026-10-28, way-to route ends
across houses; the owner's choice (b) of 10-28).

Against protomaps/basemaps at ca93fc06efbaff1c5f069d06edbe5de18839c1c8 (tiles 4.15.2), with 0001, 0002 and 0003
already applied. Applied after them with `git apply` by map-build/bin/build-basemap-jar.sh.

The app reads fence coverage tile by tile. A zoom-15 tile with a barriers layer was built with barriers, so no
fence line in it means no fence is mapped there. A tile without the layer was built before this, so fences were
not checked. Without a mark, a tile with no fence has no barriers layer at all (MVT drops empty layers), and so
looks the same as a tile from before 0003.

The mark: one point at the tile's corner with no id and no fields, added by Barriers as a TilePostProcessor
(ForwardingProfile.postProcessTileFeatures at planetiler 0.10.2) to every zoom-15 tile Planetiler writes, after
the layers' own post-processing. A point with no fields is the smallest feature MVT can hold. The app's reader
ignores points in this layer, since barriers are lines.

Pinned by three more forager* cases in BarriersTest (8 in all).

